cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A2L Update Tool: retrieval-augmented semantic alignment for automotive ECU calibration description updates"
message: "If you use this tool, the A2L-RAGAlign method, or the accompanying ISCAS 2027 submission, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Wang"
    given-names: "Wei"
    affiliation: "East China Normal University"
  - family-names: "Du"
    given-names: "Dehui"
    affiliation: "East China Normal University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jack0430-dev/A2L-RAGAlign_2026"
url: "https://github.com/jack0430-dev/A2L-RAGAlign_2026"
abstract: >-
  Automated regeneration of ASAM MCD-2A A2L description files from binary
  address files (AXF/ELF/MAP), with retrieval-augmented semantic alignment
  (A2L-RAGAlign) for calibration and measurement description updates.
  The tool recovers object types, enumerations, struct members and array
  shapes from DWARF, preserves the user's original A2L header byte-for-byte,
  and emits per-signal evidence so that unmatched signals are visible rather
  than silent. The whole pipeline is available headless for CI and
  reproducible experiments.
keywords:
  - A2L
  - ASAM MCD-2A
  - automotive calibration
  - ECU
  - INCA
  - CANape
  - DWARF
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - semantic alignment
license: MIT
version: "2.7"
